{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1004", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you make a kayak training session on flat water of about 1.5h\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here is a training session for flat water kayaking that takes about 1.5 hours:\\n \\n\\n Warm up: 10 minute paddle around the lake, working on your stroke technique and paddle strokes\\n \\n\\n Main Set:\\n \\n\\n -  20 minute paddle across the lake, practicing kayak handling skills such as turning, stopping, and starting\\n -  20 minute interval paddling drills, practicing your stroke technique and building endurance\\n -  10 minute paddle around the lake, cooling down and stretching\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you incorporate a ball in this training\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you can use a small rubber ball or volleyball to practice some kayak drills, such as passing the ball from one hand to the other while paddling. You can also play some fun kayak games using the ball, such as basketball or volleyball. This can add some variety to your training and help you improve your paddle strokes.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat's a fun game to play while kayakking that takes about half an hour\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOne fun kayak game to play is paddle polo. The goal is to score goals by shooting the ball into the opponent's net using your paddle. You can play against a friend or in teams, and the game takes about 30 minutes to play. It is a great way to get some exercise while having fun.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat's another fun game\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAnother fun kayak game to play is kayak tug of war. In this game, two teams of kayakers try to pull each other's boat across the lake, while trying to maintain their position in their own boat. It is a fun competition that takes about 15-20 minutes to play.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nanother one\", \"response\": \"Another fun kayak game is kayak jousting. In this game, two kayakers face off against each other in a race to see who can knock their opponent out of their boat using a paddle. It is a fun and challenging game that takes about 15-20 minutes to play.\\n \\n\\n Here are some tips for playing kayak jousting:\\n \\n\\n 1. Choose a calm, flat body of water for the game.\\n 2. Each player should wear a life jacket for safety.\\n 3. Each player should have a paddle with a flat, sturdy blade.\\n 4. The players should start the game by facing each other, with their boats about 10-15 feet apart.\\n 5. The goal is to use the paddle to knock the other player out of their boat without being knocked out yourself.\\n 6. The player who remains in their boat for the longest time wins the game.\\n 7. To increase the challenge, players can try to use different paddle strokes and techniques to try to knock each other out of their boats.\\n 8. The game can be played in rounds, with the winner of each round advancing to the next round.\\n 9. It is important to stay focused and maintain good balance while playing kayak jousting.\\n 10. Have fun and be safe while playing this challenging and exciting game!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/75", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how to get help finding subsidized housing for someone in recovery in seattle\\n\", \"response\": \"Here are some steps you can take to help someone in recovery find subsidized housing in Seattle:\\n\\n1. Reach out to local housing authorities: The Seattle Housing Authority is responsible for providing affordable housing to low-income families, individuals, and families. You can contact them to learn about their housing programs and how to apply.\\n\\n2. Look for affordable housing options: There are several affordable housing options in Seattle that provide housing for people in recovery. Some of these options include:\\n\\n- Public housing: Public housing is managed by the Seattle Housing Authority and provides affordable housing to low-income families.\\n\\n- Section 8 housing: Section 8 housing is a government program that provides rental assistance to low-income families, individuals, and families.\\n\\n- Affordable housing developments: There are several affordable housing developments in Seattle that provide housing for people in recovery. These developments often have specific requirements and policies related to recovery.\\n\\n- Supportive housing: Supportive housing is housing that provides additional services to help people maintain their recovery. This can include on-site support services, such as counseling, case management, and addiction treatment.\\n\\n3. Work with a housing counselor: Housing counselors can provide assistance and guidance in finding affordable housing. They can help you navigate the housing application process, understand your rights as a tenant, and provide advice on how to budget and manage your finances.\\n\\n4. Connect with recovery support services: Recovery support services can provide valuable resources and support for someone in recovery. These services can help connect individuals with housing options, support groups, and other resources that can help them maintain their recovery.\\n\\n5. Look for housing-specific resources: There are several organizations and resources in Seattle that specialize in providing housing for people in recovery. Some of these resources include:\\n\\n- The Recovery Housing Coalition: The Recovery Housing Coalition provides resources and support for people in recovery who are looking for affordable housing. They offer a directory of recovery-friendly housing options in Seattle.\\n\\n- The Center for Community Recovery: The Center for Community Recovery provides housing and support services for people in recovery. They offer a range of services, including housing assistance, recovery support, and job training.\\n\\n- The Seattle Recovery Alliance: The Seattle Recovery Alliance provides resources and support for people in recovery, including housing assistance and recovery support services. They offer a directory of recovery-friendly housing options in Seattle.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can help someone in recovery find affordable and supportive housing in Seattle.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/938", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"From now you will act as a University student. A University student is a person who doesn't know much and is trying learn more. A University student is a human. When given questions you will be answering like a University student. Remember a University student follows the rules in the questions given and he is does then step by step in a brief human language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAlright, I’m ready to be a University student. What are the questions?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n1)Describe the link between a professional & ethical consultancy team & success of the consultancy business. (8 Marks\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWell, having a well-trained and ethical team of consultants is essential for the success of a consultancy business, as it ensures that the company can provide high-quality services to clients. A strong ethical code also helps to ensure that the consultancy team operates in a fair and transparent manner, which can improve the company’s reputation and increase its customer base. Finally, a professional consultancy team can improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the consultancy business, which can boost the company’s profits.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n2) Explain how physical location influences the success of a consultancy firm. (6 Marks)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe location of a consultancy firm can impact its success in several ways. First of all, a firm located in a major city or metropolitan area will generally have access to a larger pool of clients, which can boost its revenue. In addition, being located in a desirable area can help a consultancy attract and retain talented consultants, which can improve the quality of its services. Finally, a consultancy located in a desirable area may be more appealing to potential clients, which can increase its customer base.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n3) explain approaches that can me used to carry out a market survey to establish the level of demand for certain ICT services. (8 Marks)\", \"response\": \"There are various approaches that can be used to carry out a market survey to establish the level of demand for ICT services. Here are a few examples:\\n \\n\\n 1. Surveys: A survey is a questionnaire distributed to a sample of the population to gather information about their attitudes, opinions, and behaviors. For example, an online survey can be conducted to gather feedback from potential customers about their needs and preferences for certain ICT services.\\n \\n\\n 2. Focus groups: Focus groups are organized discussions involving a small group of participants, typically 8-10 people, who are asked questions about their attitudes and opinions towards certain products or services. Focus groups can help to gather in-depth information about the needs and preferences of potential customers.\\n \\n\\n 3. Online analytics: Online analytics tools such as Google Analytics can be used to track website traffic and user behavior, providing insights into customer needs and preferences. For example, if a website offers a range of ICT services, analyzing the pages that receive the most traffic may reveal which services are most popular with customers.\\n \\n\\n 4. Social media listening: Social media listening involves monitoring social media platforms to gather information about customers' needs and preferences. For example, analyzing social media posts and comments can provide insights into customer needs and pain points, which can be used to inform the development of new ICT services.\\n \\n\\n 5. Customer interviews: One-on-one interviews with customers can provide valuable insights into their needs and preferences. Interviews can be conducted over the phone, via video conferencing, or in person, and can be structured or unstructured depending on the objectives of the market survey.\\n \\n\\n 6. Competitive analysis: Analyzing the services offered by competitors can provide insights into customer needs and preferences. For example, if a competitor offers a particular ICT service that is popular with customers, there may be a demand for similar services in the market.\\n \\n\\n 7. Tradeshows and industry events: Attending tradeshows and industry events can provide an opportunity to gather information about customer needs and preferences. Participating in panel discussions, giving presentations, and networking with industry professionals can help to gather insights into customer needs and preferences.\\n \\n\\n 8. Market research reports: Market research reports can provide insights into customer needs and preferences. These reports often contain data and analysis on market trends, customer behavior, and competition, which can be used to inform the development of new ICT services.\\n \\n\\n By employing a mix of these approaches, a consultancy firm can gather comprehensive information about the demand for certain ICT services, which can help to inform their strategic decisions and ensure their success in the market.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/918", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain HTML\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHTML is a web-markup language that is used to describe the content of web pages. HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language, and it is used to structure the text, images, and other content of web pages, and to specify how different elements of the page should be displayed. HTML is written in plain text, and uses a simple set of tags to mark up the different elements of the page. HTML can be created using a WYSIWYG editor, or manually.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat does WYSIWYG stand for? What are the two main advantages of\\n using WYSIWYG editors?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWYSIWYG stands for What You See Is What You Get. WYSIWYG editors allow you to create HTML documents without having to learn HTML. This makes it very easy to create simple web pages, and WYSIWYG editors often include visual aids that help you to position content within the page. WYSIWYG editors are also very fast and easy to use, and they allow you to create complex web pages quickly and without any prior knowledge of HTML. The two main advantages of using WYSIWYG editors are that they are very easy to use, and they allow you to create complex web pages quickly and without any prior knowledge of HTML.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is the difference between container elements and empty\\n elements?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nContainer elements are HTML elements that have content within them, such as the <p> and <ol> elements. Empty elements are elements that have no content within them, such as the <br> and <hr> elements. Container elements are generally used to enclose other elements, while empty elements are generally used to create simple formatting effects.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nList any four rules of writing HTML code\", \"response\": \"Here are four rules for writing HTML code:\\n \\n\\n 1. Use correct syntax: HTML has a specific syntax that must be followed in order for the code to be recognized by web browsers.\\n \\n\\n 2. Use semantic markup: Semantic markup helps to describe the meaning of the content on a page, making it easier for both users and search engines to understand the structure and purpose of the page.\\n \\n\\n 3. Use consistent indentation: Indentation helps to make the code more readable and easier to understand.\\n \\n\\n 4. Use meaningful element names: Use element names that accurately describe the content they contain, and avoid using generic names like \\\"div\\\" or \\\"span\\\" unless they are truly generic.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1033", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"It's 2023. President trump is no longer president. Joe Biden (D) is now president. Former president trump has been indicted for paying hush money to a former stripper to keep her silent. Provide an outline with talking points on how to discuss this with a group of 8th grade students.\", \"response\": \"Here is an outline with talking points on how to discuss the news about former President Trump with a group of 8th-grade students:\\n\\n1. Introduction: Start by introducing the topic and explaining that news has emerged about former President Trump being indicted.\\n\\n2. Understanding the situation: Explain to the students that the indictment relates to allegations of paying hush money to a former stripper to keep her silent during his time in office. Discuss the importance of understanding the legal system and the concept of justice.\\n\\n3. Ethics and morality: This is an opportunity to discuss ethics and morality in politics. Discuss the importance of honesty and integrity in public officials and the impact that unethical behavior can have on society.\\n\\n4. The role of the president: Explain the role of the president as the leader of the country and the importance of setting a positive example for others. Discuss the values and behaviors that should be upheld by a president.\\n\\n5. The legal system: Discuss the role of the legal system in our society and the importance of following the law. Explain that everyone is innocent until proven guilty and that the justice system is designed to ensure that everyone is treated fairly.\\n\\n6. Freedom of the press: Discuss the importance of freedom of the press and the role of the media in reporting news. Explain that it is important to seek out reliable sources and to be respectful of different perspectives.\\n\\n7. Conclusion: End the discussion by encouraging the students to form their own opinions based on the information they have learned. Encourage them to be respectful of different viewpoints and to always strive to make informed decisions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/719", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write outline of report about air-prunning pots.\", \"response\": \"I. Introduction\\n\\nA. Definition of Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nB. Importance of Air-Pruning Pots in Plant Growth\\n\\nC. Purpose of the Report\\n\\nII. What are Air-Pruning Pots?\\n\\nA. Explanation of how air-pruning pots work\\n\\nB. Comparison with traditional pots\\n\\nC. Benefits of using air-pruning pots\\n\\nIII. Types of Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nA. Fabric Pots\\n\\nB. Plastic Pots\\n\\nC. Other Materials\\n\\nIV. How to Use Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nA. Choosing the right size and material\\n\\nB. Planting process\\n\\nC. Maintenance and care\\n\\nV. Case Studies\\n\\nA. Example 1: Growing tomatoes in air-pruning pots\\n\\nB. Example 2: Using air-pruning pots for indoor plants\\n\\nVI. Conclusion\\n\\nA. Summary of key points\\n\\nB. Final thoughts on the benefits of air-pruning pots\\n\\nVII. References\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/36", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a Alexa developer advocate and software engineer writing a conference talk proposal. I will give you a topic and information you can use to write a talk.\\n\\nWrite an talk proposal about how to build Alexa Widgets using the Alexa Presentation Language (APL). The audience is android and web developers that want to reach new customers on the Echo Show 15 device. Because on the Echo Show 15 you can customize the home screen with widgets to create a tailored home screen experience. For developer this allow their apps to surface tangible information for users when they need it.\", \"response\": \"Title: \\\"Building Alexa Widgets with APL: A New Way for Android and Web Developers to Reach Customers on the Echo Show 15\\\"\\n\\nAbstract:\\nThe Echo Show 15 is the latest addition to the Amazon Alexa family, offering a new way for users to interact with their favorite apps and services. As a developer, you can now create Alexa Widgets that surface tangible information for users on the Echo Show 15's home screen. In this talk, we'll explore how to build Alexa Widgets using the Alexa Presentation Language (APL).\\n\\nObjective:\\nThe goal of this talk is to provide Android and web developers with the knowledge and tools they need to create engaging APL-based widgets for the Echo Show 15. By doing so, you'll be able to reach new customers and provide them with a tailored home screen experience.\\n\\nOutline:\\n\\nIntroduction to APL and Alexa Widgets\\n- What is APL?\\n- How do Alexa Widgets work?\\n- Advantages of using APL to build widgets for the Echo Show 15\\nCreating an APL-based widget\\n- Setting up the development environment\\n- Writing the APL code for your widget\\n- Integrating your widget with the Alexa Skills Kit\\nOptimizing your widget for the Echo Show 15\\n- Tips for designing responsive and interactive widgets\\n- Best practices for using animations, transitions, and gestures\\n- Considerations for localization and internationalization\\nCase studies and real-world examples\\n- Showcase successful APL-based widgets from other developers\\n- Discuss lessons learned and best practices from real-world implementations\\nFuture of APL and Alexa Widgets\\n- Planned improvements and new features for APL\\n- Potential new devices and platforms for APL-based widgets\\nConclusion:\\nBuilding Alexa Widgets with APL is an exciting new opportunity for Android and web developers to reach customers on the Echo Show 15. By creating engaging and interactive widgets, you can provide users with a tailored home screen experience and drive engagement with your app or service. Join this talk to learn the ins and outs of building APL-based widgets and start reaching new customers today!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/275", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How to generate a CSV with python that contains stock price of AAPL each minute for the last two years?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe best way to do this is to use an API, which is a program that allows you to access data from another program. The best API for this purpose is probably Alpha Vantage, which provides a function for you to call that returns a stock quote. You would need to make a call to that function once every minute for the last two years, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. You could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCould you give me an example with another API to obtain prices each minute?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I could use the Yahoo Finance API instead. I would define an end_date and a start_date, and then make a call to the Yahoo Finance API once every minute between the start_date and the end_date, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. I could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhy you defined end_date and start_date if never are used?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI defined the start_date and end_date so that I could use them in a filter, to limit the data that the Yahoo Finance API returned. I didn’t actually use the filter, though, because I wanted to make sure I got all the data I needed.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncould you give me an example using end_date and start_date and splitting the request for day?\", \"response\": \"Sure, I could use the Yahoo Finance API to get stock prices for a single day, and then use the start_date and end_date to limit the data that the Yahoo Finance API returned. I would define a start_date and an end_date, and then make a call to the Yahoo Finance API once every minute between the start_date and the end_date, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. I could then save the list as a CSV file.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/534", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a product roadmap about a network management system which is used to manage and monitor a layer 1 network device \", \"response\": \"Here is a sample product roadmap for a network management system used to manage and monitor a layer 1 network device:\\n\\nPhase 1: Discovery and Planning\\n\\nConduct market research to identify customer needs and pain points in managing layer 1 network devices\\nIdentify key features and functionalities that customers require in a network management system\\nDevelop a high-level product vision and strategy\\nCreate a product roadmap outlining the key features and milestones for the first version of the product\\nPhase 2: Development and Testing\\n\\nDevelop a minimum viable product (MVP) with core features such as device discovery, configuration management, and performance monitoring\\nConduct user testing to gather feedback and refine the product\\nAdd additional features such as real-time alerting, network mapping, and security management\\nConduct further testing to ensure the product is stable and reliable\\nPhase 3: Launch and Support\\n\\nLaunch the product to the market and gather feedback from early adopters\\nProvide customer support and training to ensure a smooth onboarding process\\nContinuously gather feedback and make improvements to the product based on customer needs\\nPhase 4: Growth and Expansion\\n\\nExpand the product offering to support additional network devices and protocols\\nDevelop integrations with other network management tools to provide a more comprehensive solution\\nExplore new markets and customer segments to expand the customer base\\nContinuously innovate and add new features to stay ahead of the competition\\nPhase 5: Maintenance and Support\\n\\nProvide ongoing maintenance and support to ensure the product remains stable and reliable\\nAddress any security vulnerabilities and compliance requirements\\nContinuously monitor the market and make updates to the product roadmap as needed\\nThis roadmap provides a high-level overview of the key phases and milestones in developing a network management system for layer 1 network devices. The specific features and timelines may vary based on the needs of the target market and the resources available to the development team.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"licens